    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126-a3">

                <pb facs="0312" n="264" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg264"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 194.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Allen Young to
                        Mr. Pierrepont.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>12, <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Stratton Street</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1877-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            10, 1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that, with
                    reference to the desire of the lords commissioners of admiralty, I have great
                    pleasure in forwarding the relics of the United States exploring ship Polaris,
                    which I found on Littleton Island last autumn, and brought to England in the
                    Pandora.</p>
                <p>The records of Captain Harstene, United States Navy, which I also found on
                    Sutherland Island, have already been transmitted to the United States
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ALLEN YOUNG.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards Pierrepont</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
